{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And now what have I here.</b> Furthermore, by way of illustration as in the language of people, or: what have I that I should be silent:" "<b>For My people are taken for nothing.</b> In Babylon and in Edom and in every nation:" "<b>And their rulers.</b> These are the great ones of Israel, and the correct reading is that it is like על כן יאמרו המושלים באה חשבון (Numbers 21:27):" "<b>Howl.</b> With the heh of the [hithpa'el] binyan shown:" "<b>Blasphemed.</b> The tav is swallowed, and likewise הוא מתנואץ:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:10.075722629Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}